From: Linux psX contributors <noreply@ps4-linux>
Subject: [PATCH] x86/ps4: default PCI windows and interrupt remapping for Baikal

Apply the documented pci=nocrs and intremap=off platform policy without
requiring the loader to supply these options. A runtime PS4 accessor keeps
normal PC boots unchanged; compiling X86_PS4 alone is insufficient.

Set the PCI default before the existing explicit-command-line checks, so
pci=use_crs still overrides it. Track explicit intremap=on/off and
nointremap choices before applying the interrupt-remapping default. Other
intremap modifiers do not implicitly enable remapping.

This is a new Linux psX addition for the 7.2 Baikal native target. It does
not change root selection, display, SATA policy or the loader command line.
Related report: https://github.com/meerzulee/linux-psx/issues/8
No hardware acceptance is claimed.
---
